meta {
  name: Update Profile
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{apiUrl}}/users/me
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "skillLevel": 3
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.success: eq true
  res.body.data.skillLevel: eq 3
}

docs {
  Implemented: `UpdateProfileUseCase` + `UpdateProfileDto`, `UserRepository.update` as an
  `UpdateCommand` with `ConditionExpression: attribute_exists(PK)`.

  This is the *only* way `skillLevel` ever changes -- it's not a Cognito attribute, so
  there's no JWT claim to fall back on; it exists solely in the `USER#` DynamoDB item.

  Known gap this does **not** fix: `user_name` already denormalized onto existing
  sessions/requests stays stale after this call -- the Streams-based sync in
  `DATABASE_DESIGN.md` is still unbuilt. Only *future* sessions/requests pick up the new name.
}
